rem Pizza Toppings
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=281
rem Sum the numbers f(m, n) of pizzas
rem of m n slices with m toppings on n
rem slices each, up to rotation, that
rem are at most Limit

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 1000000000000000
option MaxM integer = 40
option MaxN integer = 60

rem By Burnside's lemma f(m, n) is the
rem sum of phi(t) (m n / t)! /
rem ((n / t)!)^m over the divisors t of
rem n, divided by m n. Pairs are tried
rem in a box big enough for the limit.
Facts' = 1 to (MaxM * MaxN)
Fact = Facts scan * with 1
Answer = 0
for M in 2 to MaxM
  for N in 1 to MaxN
    Ts = N divisors array
    Total = 0
    for I in 0 till (Ts len)
      T = Ts I
      Ks' = 1 to T array
      Coprime' = Ks gcd T equal 1
      Ph = Coprime count
      Top = Fact (M * N // T)
      Bot = Fact (N // T) ** M
      Total += Ph * (Top // Bot)
    end
    F = Total // (M * N)
    if F at most Limit
      Answer += F
    end
  end
end
Answer print
